CamSniff on Debian
==================

CamSniff orchestrates several network scanners and packet capture utilities. On
Debian systems the binary is shipped without elevated privileges; interactive
runs should be executed with `sudo camsniff` or equivalent capabilities so that
Masscan and TShark integrations succeed.  See `/usr/share/doc/camsniff/` for
packaged guides on mode configuration and extending the data dictionaries.

The package build runs the focused regression suite and shell syntax checks in
CI.  Live network tests are intentionally omitted from package builds; release
smoke tests use an isolated loopback-only network namespace instead.

Packaged runs default to `/var/lib/camsniff/results/`.  Reports are redacted,
but `credentials.json` and captured media remain sensitive and owner-readable.
